{
  "date": "2026-10-27",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "金价回落，银行买入积存金要先重新测评风险",
  "title_en": "Gold Falls Back: Banks Ask Customers to Retake Risk Assessment Before Buying Gold Savings Plans",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "10月23日，国际现货黄金价格一度跌到每盎司4000美元以下，最低是3975美元。到10月26日，金价大约是4011美元，比今年的最高点低了百分之二十九左右。",
      "en": "On October 23, the international spot gold price briefly fell below 4,000 US dollars per ounce, with a low of 3,975 dollars. By October 26, gold was at about 4,011 dollars, roughly 29 percent below this year's peak."
    },
    {
      "zh": "国内金价也回落到每克八百多元。银行的积存金是一种买黄金的方式，客户可以定期用少量的钱买入黄金。",
      "en": "Gold prices in China also fell back to a little over 800 yuan per gram. A bank's gold savings plan (积存金) is a way to buy gold: customers can regularly use a small amount of money to buy gold."
    },
    {
      "zh": "第一财经的记者发现，有客户打开银行App想买入，却看到风险测评已经过期，要重新做测评才能继续。",
      "en": "Yicai reporters found that some customers opened their bank app wanting to buy, but saw that their risk assessment had expired and they had to take it again before they could continue."
    },
    {
      "zh": "另外，很多银行把买入费率降到零，但是卖出的费用和买卖差价没有明显变化。",
      "en": "In addition, many banks cut their buying fee rate to zero, but the selling fees and the buy–sell price gap have not changed noticeably."
    }
  ],
